tools.description:
Run JavaScript that calls the tools listed below and return what it prints. Use it to gather and condense in one call what would take several tool calls, such as checking every task and reporting only the ones that need attention, or waiting on several tasks at once.

The code is an ES module body: top-level await works. Print what you want back with text(value) or console.log(value); objects print as JSON, and nothing else is returned. Each tool takes one object argument and resolves with its structured result; a failed call rejects with its error. The script runs in an isolated sandbox with no files, network, modules, require, process or fetch: these tools are its only way out. Pass long text through `inputs` and read it as inputs.<name>. Errors report the line and column in your code.

Tools:
// List the coding agents you can hand tasks to with start_task, such as Claude Code and Codex.
tools.list_agents(): Promise<{ agents: { id: string; is_you: boolean; name: string }[] }>
// List the tasks you can reach, with their status: the tasks you started and, if you are a task yourself, the task that started you ("parent") and its other tasks (your siblings).
tools.list_tasks(): Promise<{ tasks: { agent: string; id: string; relation: "parent" | "child" | "sibling"; status: "running" | "needs_approval" | "idle" | "failed" | "cancelled" | "closed"; title?: string }[]; you?: string }>
// Wait for a task's current turn to finish, then return its status and its reply: what the agent said at the end of its latest turn.
tools.wait_for_task(input: { task_id: string; timeout_seconds?: number }): Promise<{ agent: string; detail?: string; relation: "parent" | "child" | "sibling"; reply?: string; status: "running" | "needs_approval" | "idle" | "failed" | "cancelled"; task_id: string; title?: string }>
// Check a task's status and its latest reply without waiting.
tools.get_task(input: { task_id: string }): Promise<{ agent: string; detail?: string; relation: "parent" | "child" | "sibling"; reply?: string; status: "running" | "needs_approval" | "idle" | "failed" | "cancelled"; task_id: string; title?: string }>
